                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A game with some interesting mechanics, a leveling system, and so on, but its physics are very clunky, let alone the user experience design which I find terrible. Some dynamics aren't even understandable, the puzzles are very unintuitive, and at times it becomes a walking simulator (out of the 16 hours of gameplay, I must have spent 5 just walking). The sound design is really good, the graphics are decent, and the story isn't bad. It also has a few bugs and, for God's sake, the pointless jump scares. In short, it feels like a game that wasn't given any love—they just threw a bunch of elements into a bag and this came out. It needs a lot of polishing to be an enjoyable experience.",
